# =============================================================================
# PETRICHOR — Assets/Art/.gitignore
# =============================================================================
# Art-pipeline-specific ignores.
#
# The root .gitignore covers Unity GENERATED state (Library/, Temp/, build
# output). This file covers what a PURCHASED art pipeline leaves behind: vendor
# source archives, authoring-tool documents, and preview renders.
#
# Why a second file rather than more lines in the root: these rules govern one
# directory, and a rule that lives next to the thing it governs survives a
# refactor. Git applies a .gitignore to its own directory and everything below
# it, so these patterns are relative to Assets/Art/.
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md section 6 for the LFS policy, and the repository-rules
# page for the storage budget these rules exist to protect.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Vendor source archives
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purchased packs arrive as an archive. The archive is re-downloadable from the
# vendor and is the single largest thing in the pipeline, so it never enters
# git. The IMPORTED assets below are what gets committed.
/_vendor/
/_downloads/
*.7z
*.rar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Authoring-tool documents
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are the editable sources behind a texture or a mesh. They are large,
# they are not read by Unity, and they are only useful to whoever is authoring
# the asset. The exported result (.png, .fbx) is what the project needs.
*.sbs            # Substance Designer source
*.spp            # Substance Painter project
*.ztl            # ZBrush tool
*.zpr            # ZBrush project
*.psb            # Photoshop large document
*.blend1         # Blender backup
*.blend2
*.ma~            # Maya backup
*.mb~
*.hip            # Houdini scene
*.hipnc
*.mview          # Marmoset viewer
*.spm            # SpeedTree model source
*.tgd            # Terragen project
*.gproj          # Gaea project
*.wcproj         # World Creator project

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Preview renders and thumbnails
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by the vendor or by the authoring tool for browsing. Regenerable,
# and there are hundreds of them.
/_previews/
/_thumbnails/
*.thumb.png
*.preview.jpg

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Megascans and similar library caches
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Quixel/Bridge local library is a cache of re-downloadable content. The
# assets the project actually uses are copied into the category folders and
# committed from there.
/_megascans/
/_bridge/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Import staging
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where a pack is unpacked before its assets are sorted into Terrain/,
# Vegetation/, Rock/, Water/, Props/ and Sky/. Transient by definition.
/_staging/
/_unsorted/
